  "format": "From the hazard archive (650 MB), the reduced-resolution overviews (.ovr, GDAL's external overviews of the 1 m depth rasters) of river (FLRF) and surface-water (FLSW) flooding at each return period, read by range requests as zip members; the full 1 m rasters are not fetched. The modelled portfolio (Freetown_ptf_v2.csv: each building's latitude, longitude, occupancy and insured value in US dollars). The Oasis loss outputs: average annual loss (aalcalc), event loss table (eltcalc), aggregate and occurrence exceedance curves (leccalc), year loss table (pltcalc), by occupancy (S1) and for the 1 m area (S2). Average annual loss by ward (shapefile), and the City Council's flash-flood points and areas.",
  "coverage": "Freetown's 1 m DEM area; modelled river and surface-water flooding, baseline climate, undefended.",
  "licence": "CC BY 4.0 (World Bank Data Catalog)",
  "citation": "World Bank (2023), Freetown, Sierra Leone Flood Risk Assessment, https://datacatalog.worldbank.org/search/dataset/0066934.",
